From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:58:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWebView: Let a WebAuthn request follow one that has been
 answered

When an authenticator says it already holds one of the excluded
credentials, the coordinator rejects the page's create() with an
InvalidStateError right away, and keeps the ceremony only so that
its prompt can tell the user. That ceremony still counted as the
tab's request in progress, so a request the page made as soon as it
had the error was rejected with "Another WebAuthn request is in
progress", for as long as the user left the prompt up.

With virtual authenticators, nobody is there to close the prompt,
and the ceremony ends from a deferred invocation instead. But a
connection handles every message it has read when it gets to them,
so a follow-up request read in the same pass of the event loop
could still get there first, and WebAuthn/create-and-get.html
failed now and then.

A ceremony that has answered the page now makes way for the tab's
next request: it ends, closing its prompt, and the new one starts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Libraries/LibWebView/WebAuthn/Coordinator.cpp | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWebView/WebAuthn/Coordinator.cpp b/Libraries/LibWebView/WebAuthn/Coordinator.cpp
index 58a5f51d3053c782ffa546c2072a821e048ce014..0f2690f98536fd3d57aa0aa6f1bdaf0449f95507 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWebView/WebAuthn/Coordinator.cpp
+++ b/Libraries/LibWebView/WebAuthn/Coordinator.cpp
@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@ public:
     WebContentPage* page() const { return m_page.ptr(); }
     u64 request_id() const { return m_request_id; }
     bool is_create() const { return m_request.has<CreateRequest>(); }
+    bool has_answered() const { return m_phase == Phase::Answered; }
 
     ViewImplementation* view() const
     {
@@ -878,9 +879,15 @@ void WebAuthnCoordinator::begin(WebContentPage& page, u64 request_id, CeremonyCo
         }
     }
 
-    if (any_of(m_ceremonies, [&](auto const& ceremony) { return ceremony->page() && &ceremony->page()->traversable() == &traversable; })) {
-        page.async_web_authn_request_completed(request_id, not_allowed("Another WebAuthn request is in progress"sv));
-        return;
+    if (auto index = m_ceremonies.find_first_index_if([&](auto const& ceremony) { return ceremony->page() && &ceremony->page()->traversable() == &traversable; }); index.has_value()) {
+        auto& ceremony = *m_ceremonies[*index];
+        if (!ceremony.has_answered()) {
+            page.async_web_authn_request_completed(request_id, not_allowed("Another WebAuthn request is in progress"sv));
+            return;
+        }
+        // NB: A ceremony that has answered the renderer keeps its prompt up only to inform the user, and the renderer
+        //     may make its next request as soon as it has the answer, so the ceremony makes way for that request.
+        ceremony.end({});
     }
 
     auto ceremony = adopt_ref(*new Ceremony(page, request_id, move(context), move(request)));
